# THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 18 — CHAPTERS 26-28 (LEAN, 2026-09-26): chapter 26's Sifrei rows TYPED, piska 301 rows 19-37 (on 26:8-11): the mighty hand the
# pestilence, the arm the sword, the terror the Shekhinah, the signs the staff, the wonders the blood, the ten plagues by pairs and R. Judah's mnemonic; this place
# the Temple, milk and honey the five nations and not Trans-Jordan; now, behold, I have brought; the early fig tied with reed; who brings and does not recite; the
# two settings; every kind of joy, the song; the wife's property; the confessors. Every row READ WHOLE in both files; the cuts by ch26_ink.SP_. Sitting 17's form.
from ch26_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(301, 19, 'MATERIAL', f'"WITH A MIGHTY HAND" (26:8) — THIS IS THE PESTILENCE, AS IT IS WRITTEN "BEHOLD THE HAND OF THE LORD IS ON YOUR CATTLE IN THE FIELD … A VERY GRIEVOUS PESTILENCE" (EXODUS 9:3). ({SP_(301, 19, "זו", "הדבר")} "this is the pestilence"; {SP_(301, 19, "הויה", "במקנך", "אשר", "בשדה")} "is upon your cattle in the field"): the hand the fifth plague — Exodus 9:3\'s own "hand". Fresh.')
srow(301, 20, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND WITH AN OUTSTRETCHED ARM" — THIS IS THE SWORD, AS IT IS WRITTEN "WITH HIS SWORD DRAWN IN HIS HAND, OUTSTRETCHED" (JOSHUA 5:13). ({SP_(301, 20, "זו", "החרב")} "this is the sword"; {SP_(301, 20, "וחרבו", "שלופה", "בידו", "נטויה")} "and his sword drawn in his hand, outstretched"): the arm the sword by Joshua\'s captain (the Prophets\' seat, not read ahead). Fresh.')
srow(301, 21, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND WITH GREAT TERROR" — THIS IS THE REVELATION OF THE SHEKHINAH, AS IT IS WRITTEN "HAS ANY GOD TRIED TO COME AND TAKE HIM A NATION FROM THE MIDST OF A NATION BY TRIALS, SIGNS, WONDERS, WAR, A MIGHTY HAND, AN OUTSTRETCHED ARM AND GREAT TERRORS, AS ALL THE LORD YOUR GOD DID FOR YOU IN EGYPT BEFORE YOUR EYES" (4:34). ({SP_(301, 21, "זו", "גלוי", "שכינה")} "this is the revelation of the Shekhinah"; {SP_(301, 21, "במסות", "באותות", "ובמופתים", "ובמלחמה")} "by trials, by signs, by wonders and by war"): THE TERROR THE PRESENCE — 4:34\'s list the ground (Onkelos at 26:8: "a great vision"). REREAD WHOLE (chapter 4, deu_04_vaetchanan).')
srow(301, 22, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND WITH SIGNS" — THIS IS THE STAFF, AS IT IS WRITTEN "AND THIS STAFF YOU SHALL TAKE IN YOUR HAND, WITH WHICH YOU SHALL DO THE SIGNS" (EXODUS 4:17). ({SP_(301, 22, "זה", "המטה")} "this is the staff"; {SP_(301, 22, "אשר", "תעשה", "בו", "את", "האותות")} "with which you shall do the signs"): the signs the staff\'s. Fresh.')
srow(301, 23, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND WITH WONDERS" — THIS IS THE BLOOD, AS IT IS WRITTEN "I WILL SET WONDERS IN HEAVEN AND EARTH: BLOOD AND FIRE AND PILLARS OF SMOKE" (JOEL 3:3). ({SP_(301, 23, "זה", "הדם")} "this is the blood"; {SP_(301, 23, "דם", "ואש", "ותמרות", "עשן")} "blood and fire and pillars of smoke"): the wonders the blood by Joel\'s verse. Fresh.')
srow(301, 24, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD — "WITH A MIGHTY HAND" TWO, "AN OUTSTRETCHED ARM" TWO, "GREAT TERROR" TWO, "SIGNS" TWO, "WONDERS" TWO: THESE ARE THE TEN PLAGUES THE HOLY ONE BROUGHT ON THE EGYPTIANS — BLOOD, FROGS, LICE, WILD BEASTS, PESTILENCE, BOILS, HAIL, LOCUSTS, DARKNESS, THE FIRSTBORN. ({SP_(301, 24, "אלו", "עשר", "מכות")} "these are the ten plagues"; {SP_(301, 24, "דם", "צפרדע", "כנים", "ערוב", "דבר", "שחין", "ברד", "ארבה", "חשך", "מכת")} "blood, frogs, lice, beasts, pestilence, boils, hail, locusts, darkness, the plague of"): THE TEN BY PAIRS — the five phrases doubled; the last bracketed row. Fresh.')
srow(301, 25, 'MATERIAL', f'R. JUDAH GAVE THEM A SIGN: DETZAKH ADASH BEACHAV. ({SP_(301, 25, "נותן", "בהם", "סימן")} "gave them a sign"; {SP_(301, 25, "דצ״ך", "עד״ש", "באח״ב")} "the acrostic of the ten plagues\' initials"): the mnemonic — the plagues\' order fixed by their initials (the Haggadah\'s text). Fresh.')
srow(301, 26, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HE BROUGHT US TO THIS PLACE" (26:9) — THIS IS THE TEMPLE; OR THE LAND OF ISRAEL? "AND GAVE US THIS LAND" — THE LAND IS SAID; WHY "TO THIS PLACE"? BY THE MERIT OF OUR COMING TO THIS PLACE HE GAVE US THIS LAND. ({SP_(301, 26, "זה", "בית", "המקדש")} "this is the Temple"; {SP_(301, 26, "בשכר", "ביאתנו", "אל", "המקום", "הזה")} "by the reward of our coming to this place"): THE PLACE THE TEMPLE, the land its reward — the two clauses two objects. Fresh.')
srow(301, 27, 'MATERIAL', f'"A LAND FLOWING WITH MILK AND HONEY" — SAID HERE AND SAID THERE (EXODUS 13:5); THERE THE LAND OF THE FIVE NATIONS, SO HERE THE LAND OF THE FIVE NATIONS; R. YOSE THE GALILEAN: THEY DO NOT BRING FIRST-FRUITS FROM BEYOND THE JORDAN, WHICH DOES NOT FLOW WITH MILK AND HONEY. ({SP_(301, 27, "חמשת", "עממים")} "five nations"; {SP_(301, 27, "אין", "מביאים", "בכורים", "מעבר", "לירדן")} "they do not bring first-fruits from beyond the Jordan"): THE TERRITORY PARAMETER by the verbal analogy of the milk-and-honey formula with Exodus 13:5 (I2; the formula\'s fifteen Torah seats measured) — Trans-Jordan excluded (Bikkurim 1:10; 299:4 R. Simeon\'s ground beside). Fresh.')
srow(301, 28, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND NOW" (26:10) — AT ONCE. ({SP_(301, 28, "ועתה", "מיד")} "and now — at once"): the recital\'s "now" the moment of bringing. Fresh.')
srow(301, 29, 'MATERIAL', f'"BEHOLD" — IN JOY. ({SP_(301, 29, "הנה", "בשמחה")} "behold — in joy"): the particle read as the manner. Fresh.')
srow(301, 30, 'MATERIAL', f'"I HAVE BROUGHT" — FROM MY OWN. ({SP_(301, 30, "הבאתי", "משלי")} "I have brought — from my own"): the bringer\'s ownership (297:9-10\'s ground). Fresh.')
srow(301, 31, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE FIRST OF ALL THE FRUIT OF THE GROUND" — HENCE: A MAN GOES DOWN INTO HIS FIELD AND SEES A FIG THAT RIPENED FIRST, A CLUSTER, A POMEGRANATE — HE TIES IT WITH REED-GRASS AND SAYS: THESE ARE FIRST-FRUITS. ({SP_(301, 31, "יורד", "אדם", "לתוך", "שדהו", "ורואה", "תאנה", "שבכרה")} "a man goes down into his field and sees a fig that ripened first"; {SP_(301, 31, "קושרים", "אותו", "בגמי")} "they tie it with reed-grass"): THE DESIGNATION on the tree — Bikkurim 3:1 inside the spine; the compile\'s act of setting apart. Fresh.')
srow(301, 32, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHICH YOU HAVE GIVEN ME, O LORD" — HENCE: THE GUARDIAN, THE SLAVE, THE AGENT, THE WOMAN, THE TUMTUM AND THE ANDROGYNOS BRING AND DO NOT RECITE, FOR THEY CANNOT SAY "WHICH YOU HAVE GIVEN ME". ({SP_(301, 32, "האפוטרופיס", "והעבד", "והשליח", "אשה", "וטומטום", "ואנדרוגינוס", "מביאים", "ולא", "קורים")} "the guardian, the slave, the agent, a woman, the tumtum and the androgynos bring and do not recite"): THE RECITERS — six who bring without the recital, the possessive "me" the ground (Bikkurim 1:5); the compile\'s reciter parameter. Fresh.')
srow(301, 33, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND SET IT BEFORE THE LORD YOUR GOD AND BOW BEFORE THE LORD YOUR GOD" — THIS TEACHES THAT THEY REQUIRE SETTING DOWN TWICE, ONCE AT THE RECITATION AND ONCE AT THE BOWING. ({SP_(301, 33, "שטעונים", "הנחה", "שתי", "פעמים")} "they require setting down two times"): TWO SETTINGS — 26:4\'s and 26:10\'s read as two acts. Fresh.')
srow(301, 34, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL REJOICE" (26:11) — WITH EVERY KIND OF REJOICING. ({SP_(301, 34, "בכל", "מיני", "שמחות")} "with all kinds of rejoicings"): the joy unbounded in kind. Fresh.')
srow(301, 35, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN ALL THE GOOD" — THIS IS THE SONG. ({SP_(301, 35, "זה", "השיר")} "this is the song"): THE SONG at the first-fruits (Bikkurim 3:4\'s Psalm 30 the translator\'s note) — the rite\'s music a parameter. Fresh.')
srow(301, 36, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHICH THE LORD YOUR GOD HAS GIVEN YOU AND YOUR HOUSE" — THIS TEACHES THAT A MAN BRINGS FIRST-FRUITS FROM HIS WIFE\'S PROPERTY AND RECITES. ({SP_(301, 36, "מביא", "בכורים", "מנכסי", "אשתו", "וקורא")} "brings first-fruits from his wife\'s property and recites"): THE HOUSE the wife\'s field — the husband recites on it (against 301:32\'s woman who does not). Fresh.')
srow(301, 37, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU, THE LEVITE AND THE STRANGER IN YOUR MIDST" — HENCE: ISRAELITES AND BASTARDS CONFESS, BUT NOT PROSELYTES AND FREED SLAVES, WHO HAVE NO SHARE IN THE LAND. ({SP_(301, 37, "ישראל", "ממזרים", "מתודים")} "Israelites and bastards confess"; {SP_(301, 37, "שאין", "להם", "חלק", "בארץ")} "who have no share in the land"): THE CONFESSORS of the tithe (Maaser Sheni 5:14 inside the spine) — the share in the land the ground, the bastard in and the proselyte out (299:3\'s reciter parameter again). Fresh.')
